  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe cause of #2736 is a slow path. It is not a loop that does not end.\n\n- `adaptive::route::door` (in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/route.rs`) now refuses a door when the disc at the start point holds stock or wall. It refuses before it reads the leg law. Each leg capsule holds its start disc, so no leg longer than `ZERO_LEG` can pass there. The result is the same as before.\n- The other door searches read the candidate cells nearest first and stop at the first legal leg. The old search read all free cells nearer than its best cell, in raster order. The chosen cell is the same: the nearest legal cell, and the lower index on a tie.\n- `ZERO_LEG` is now one constant in `route.rs`. `lift_link::leg_ok` uses it.\n- The decision is in `docs/decisions/2736-adaptive-door-search.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\nThese are on the issue's region (the box part, area offset 3, D6, optimal load 0.5).\n\n| Build | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| release, HSM plan | 29.6 s | 9.8 s |\n| debug, HSM plan | more than 9 min (issue) | 60.2 s |\n\n- Before the fix, the microlift schedule took 23.7 s of the 29.6 s in release. In the schedule, 13 routed returns took 17 s. The door search took 16 s of that, over 53 routes. All 22 doors that failed had a blocked start disc. Each of them read the leg law on each free cell within 6 mm (grid 0.05 mm, about 58k cells).\n- Output is identical by hash on nine cases (sizes 24, 18 and 12 mm by loads 0.5, 0.35 and 0.25). The load 0.5 case keeps hash `e3a88d5d82fabc7c` and 17680 moves. The nine cases took 201 s before and 103 s after, in release.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `machining2d::adaptive::route::tests::a_door_on_stock_reads_no_leg`: a door from a point with stock in its disc gives None and reads the leg law 0 times. Before the fix it read the law 11289 times, and the test fails.\n- `machining2d::adaptive::route::tests::the_door_is_the_nearest_legal_cell`: compares `door` with the old raster-order search on five points, with a mask on the free cells and a stricter leg law.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`) on head 3074ea19b: 8 steps, 0 failed, wall 7.7 min. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The app fixture after the fix, in debug and in release. Only the motion plan was timed after the fix.\n- The tilted poses after the fix.\n- The batch gate.\n- The app plans the passes a second time when it carries the stock top. Follow-up: #2753.\n\nChangelog: 2D Adaptive plans with routed microlift returns are faster (about 3x on a small pocket at optimal load 0.5); the posted output does not change.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2736\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
